<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Monday through overnight system repurchases, analsyts said.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a reserve addition, but some had expected a three-day, rather than an overnight operation.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent at the time of the operation, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
